    { 

      "invoiceLineID": "9426589217", 

      "lineDescription": "Window washing – Building B", 

      "glCategories": ["Cleaning Services ",” Custodial Services”] 

 

     }, 

    { 

    "invoiceLineID": "94214382247",    

    "lineDescription": " INTER-COMM: COSTS/charg, C:1805 ",     

    "glCategories": ["Accounts Payables – Intercompany"] 

      } 

 ] 

} 

 

 

Fields: 

invoiceLineItemsResults: A list containing the result for each invoice line item. 

invoiceLineID: Unique identifier for the invoice line item. 

invoiceDate: Date of the invoice (YYYY-MM-DD). 

vendorID: Unique identifier for the vendor 

lineDescription: Description of the line as given by the input 

glCategories: List of all GL categories (one or more) that is suitable for the given line description 

Non-PO Invoice Similar Line Description Classification 

 

Overview 

This section outlines the expected sample input and output formats for the Non PO invoice use case pipeline. The pipeline is designed to automate the process for identifying the closest historical invoice line description, when present, based on the current invoice description. If there is no relevant description found, then it outputs “NA”. The pipeline expects one invoice in the request, processes it and generates the output.  

NOTE: The pipeline will be called only when there is no exact match found in the historical data 

